(1, 11, '1767750895633.pdf', '\n\n \n \n \nAcademic Internship Coordinator \nAuckland Institute of Studies \n28A Linwood Avenue, Mount Albert, Auckland 1025 \nSubject: Internship Opportunity for Eric Jacob at GripOnz \nDear Sir/Madam, \nI am pleased to offer an internship opportunity for Eric Jacob at GripOnz as an \nIntern at 25 College Hill, Freemans Bay, Auckland 1011. Below are the internship details: \nCompany Name & Address: \nGripOnz Limited (NZBN-9429051898960) \nRegistered Address: 26A Ayr Street Parnell, \nAuckland \nSupervisor Detail: \nAlexander Smith \nCo-Director \nSupervisor Phone: 0224301930 \nEmail: alex@griponz.com \nInternship Period: \n• Start Date: ex. Monday, 19\nth\n January \n• End Date: ex. Tuesday, 17\nth\n March 2026 \n• Duration: ex. 8 weeks (240 hours) \n• Working Hours: 30 hours per week \n• Schedule: Monday to Friday, 4:00 AM – 10:00 AM (6 hours per day) \nInternship Details: \n• Student Name & Job Title: Eric Jacobs, Finance Intern \nJob Responsibilities: \n• Financial Modelling & Forecasting of sales, new product and market potential \no Assist in building detailed financial models to support product launch and market expansion. \no Analyse revenue streams, cost structures, and profitability scenarios. \no Prepare short-term and long-term financial forecasts aligned with business objectives. \n• Budgeting & Cost Analysis \no Support the development of budgets for new product initiatives and expansion projects. \no Conduct variance analysis between actual and projected costs. \no Identify cost-saving opportunities without compromising quality or growth. \n• Market Expansion Financial Assessment \n\nBest regards, \n \no Perform financial feasibility studies for entry into the Australian market. \no Evaluate pricing strategies, regulatory costs, and competitive benchmarks. \no Prepare reports on potential ROI and risk factors for international expansion. \n• Funding & Investor Relations Support  \no Assist in preparing pitch decks and financial summaries for potential investors. \no Research funding options, including venture capital, private equity, and grants. \no Support communication with stakeholders by providing accurate financial data and insights. \nThis internship will provide Eric Jacobs with hands-on experience in financial analysis. Our team is \ncommitted to offering guidance and mentorship to support his professional growth. \nPlease feel free to reach out if you require further details. \n \nAlexander Smith \nCo-Director, GripOnz Limited ', '2026-01-07 01:54:56'),
