(23, 11, '1768371847995.docx', '\n\nAcademic Internship Coordinator\n\nAuckland Institute of Studies\n\n28A Linwood Avenue, Mount Albert, Auckland 1025\n\nInternship Opportunity for Greta Vagujhelyi at Working In\n\nDear Sir/Madam,\n\nI am pleased to offer an internship opportunity for Greta Vagujhelyi at Working In as a\n\nIntern Position at 2A Fitzroy St, Ponsonby. Auckland. Below are the internship details:\n\nCompany Name & Address: Working In New Zealand Ltd 9429045883903\n\nSupervisor Detail:\n\nJo WalshHead of Marketing & CommunicationsSupervisor Phone: 021 491 000\n\nEmail: jo.walsh@workingin.com\n\nInternship Period:\n\nStart Date: 9 Feb 2026\n\nEnd Date:   6 May 2026\n\nDuration:  12 weeks \n\nTotal hours: 240 hours\n\nWorking Hours: 20 hours per week\n\nSchedule: Monday to Friday, 9.30-1.30\n\nInternship Details:\n\nStudent Name & Job Title: Greta Vagujhelyi, Marketing Intern\n\nPurpose:To contribute to the strategic marketing and communications activities supporting our recruitment, immigration, and settlement services in New Zealand and Australia. The role will provide hands-on experience in brand strategy, campaign analysis, and international marketing planning aligned with global business objectives.\n\nKey responsibilities:\n\nAssist with developing and analysing marketing campaigns across digital and international channels – 20%/48 hours\n\nSupport brand and product strategy through market research and reporting- 15%/36 hours\n\nContribute to planning and preparing marketing materials and presentations for global audiences-20%/48 hours\n\nHelp maintain website, social media, and communication assets in line with brand strategy -25%/60 hours\n\nProvide administrative and project support, including data analysis, competitor analysis and insights to improve performance-20%/48 hours\n\n\n\nSkills and attributes:\n\nAnalytical thinking and attention to detail\n\nInterest in brand strategy, global marketing, and customer journey\n\nStrong written and verbal communication skills\n\nCollaborative and proactive approach\n\nJob Responsibilities:\n\nStrategic and brand analysis – 35% / 84 hours \n\nMarketing execution and communications – 40% / 96 hours\n\nGlobal marketing and reporting – 25% / 60 hours\n\nThis internship will provide Greta Vagujhelyi with hands-on experience in Marketing & Communications in a globally renowned business. Our team is committed to offering guidance and mentorship to support her professional growth.\n\n\n\nPlease feel free to reach out if you require further details.\n\n\n\nBest Regards\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJo Walsh\n\nHead of Marketing & Communications\n\nWorking In\n\n\n\n\n\n', '2026-01-14 06:24:08'),
(24, 11, '1768371893666.pdf', '\n\n\n\n\n\n', '2026-01-14 06:24:53'),
(25, 14, '1769593635350.pdf', '\n\nKhushba Ahmed (Kush) \nAuckland, New Zealand \nEmail: ahmedkhushba@gmail.com  \nPhone: +64 2040086953 \nGithub: https://github.com/Khushba94  \nResident Status: NZ Permanent Resident \n \nPersonal Profile \nAdaptable and detail-oriented professional transitioning into a data analyst role, with 4+ \nyears of experience in software development and current experience in internship \ncoordination. Skilled in SQL, Power BI, and Excel, with proven strengths in problem-solving, \nstakeholder communication, and data-driven decision-making. Passionate about leveraging \ntechnical expertise and analytical skills to provide insightful business solutions. \nSkills \n• Technical: PHP (Laravel, CakePHP), JavaScript, MySQL, HTML5, CSS, jQuery, \nJSON, Git, Power BI, Power Query, DAX, Microsoft Visual Studio \n• Soft Skills: Problem Solving, Team Collaboration, Communication, Time \nManagement, Customer-Focused Development \n• Familiarity: Agile Methodologies, Unit Testing, CI/CD, Cloud Services (AWS exposure \nthrough coursework), Vue.js (self-study) \nCareer History \nSoftware Developer Intern \nAuckland Institute of Studies, Auckland, NZ \nJan 2024 – Dec 2024 (1 year) \n• Built and optimized Power BI dashboards using Power Query and DAX for data \ntransformation and visualization. \n• Collaborated with teams to translate data requirements into actionable insights, \nenhancing decision-making for university management. \n• Developed interactive Power BI dashboards to visualize student enrollment data, \nimproving marketing team insights. \n• Performed data cleaning and transformation using Power Query, fostering a passion \nfor data-driven solutions. \n \nInternship Placement Coordinator \nAuckland Institute of Studies, Auckland, NZ \nFeb 2025 – Present (8 months) \n• Coordinated internship placements for MBA, Business, and IT students, with a key \nfocus on supporting IT students in securing suitable industry opportunities. \n• Managed placement data and documentation using Excel and internal systems, \nensuring accuracy and efficiency. \n• Created Power BI dashboards for the Marketing and ET teams, applying technical \nand analytical skills to improve reporting and decision-making. \n• Strengthened communication, mentoring, and problem-solving skills by working \nclosely with IT students, academic staff, and industry partners. \n\n \nSoftware Developer \nSagbrain Corporation, Auckland, NZ \nAug 2022 – Feb 2025 (2 years 7 months) \n• Developed and maintained web applications using Laravel, JavaScript, and MySQL, \nensuring scalable and testable code. \n• Implemented features, debugged issues, and conducted unit testing to maintain high \ncode quality. \n• Collaborated with cross-functional teams to deliver on sprint goals in an agile \nenvironment. \n \nSoftware Developer \nSouthern Cross Systems \nOct 2019 – Jun 2022 (2 years 9 months) \n• Built client projects using .NET, focusing on performance optimization and responsive \ndesign. \n• Supported data analysis tasks to drive business decisions, integrating user feedback \ninto development cycles. \n \nEducation \nBachelor of Computer Science and Engineering \nBRAC University, Bangladesh \n2014 – 2018, 3.79/4.0 CGPA \n• Coursework: Programming Languages, Data Structures, Algorithms, Operating \nSystems, AI \n• Achieved 100% scholarship across 9 semesters. \n \nCertifications \n• Learn JavaScript for Web Development, Udemy, Sep 2021 \nCertificate \n• Web Development, SECTOR SKILLS COUNCIL NASSCOM, Mar 2018 (Credential \nID: G047776) \n \nLanguages \n• English (Fluent), Japanese (Fluent), Bengali (Native), Hindi (Proficient). \nReferees \nReferees available on request ', '2026-01-28 09:47:15');
