(9, 11, '1768371700837.pdf', 'uploads/resumes/1768371700837.pdf', '\n\nKhushba Ahmed \nInternship Placement Coordinator \nahmedkhushba@gmail.com | Mobile: 020 4008 6953 \nAuckland, New Zealand | NZ Resident Visa \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nStudent-focused tertiary education professional with proven expertise in academic \ncoordination, compliance, and learner support. Currently serving as Internship Placement \nCoordinator at AIS, I oversee the full internship lifecycle for IT, Business, and MBA students, \nensuring alignment with academic programme requirements and institutional standards. \nSkilled in guiding students through academic processes, maintaining accurate records, \nliaising with academic leadership, and delivering clear, empathetic communication. Known \nfor organisational discipline, proactive relationship management, and a commitment to \nstudent success. \nNow seeking to contribute my coordination and education administration strengths to NZTC \nas an Enrolments Advisor.\n \nKEY SKILLS \n• Student Relationship Management & Academic Support \n• Tertiary Education Administration \n• Documentation & Compliance (NZQA-aligned) \n• Data Entry & Record Management \n• Reporting & Tracking \n• Cross-Team Coordination \n• CRM & Student Management Systems \n• Microsoft Office Suite \n \nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE \nInternship Placement Coordinator \nAuckland Institute of Studies (AIS) — Feb 2025 to Present \n• Serve as the primary point of contact for students completing the internship \ncomponent of their academic programmes. \n\n• Guide learners step-by-step through internship requirements, documentation \nstandards, approvals, deadlines, and compliance expectations. \n• Maintain accurate records for each student, ensuring documentation meets internal \nand NZQA-aligned academic standards. \n• Communicate proactively with students via email, phone, and meetings to ensure \nclarity, confidence, and smooth progression. \n• Coordinate closely with Academic Coordinators, Programme Manager, and HODs \nregarding student placement readiness, concerns, and academic requirements. \n• Update internal systems with internship data, milestones, approvals, and completion \noutcomes. \n• Prepare ad-hoc and scheduled reports on student placement progress and internship \ncompletion. \n• Support students from diverse backgrounds with patience, empathy, and cultural \nunderstanding. \n• Promote a student-first environment by resolving issues quickly and proactively \nproviding needed information. \n \nSoftware Developer | IT Administrator | Teaching Assistant (Earlier Roles) \nBangladesh, Japan & NZ — 2017 to 2025 \n• Developed software applications using PHP, Laravel, JavaScript, and modern web \ntechnologies. \n• Provided technical support, troubleshooting, and IT administration. \n• Supported academic activities, student communication, and marking workflows. \n \nEDUCATION \nBachelor of Science in Computer Science \nBRAC University \n \nREFERENCE \nAvailable upon request ', '2026-01-14 06:21:41'),
(10, 14, '1769593680656.pdf', 'uploads/resumes/1769593680656.pdf', '\n\nKhushba Ahmed (Kush) \nahmedkhushba@gmail.com | https://github.com/Khushba94 | +64 20 4008 6953 | Auckland | NZ Resident \n \nTECHNICAL SKILLS \n● Programming Languages: C#, JavaScript, VB.NET, PHP \n● Web Technologies: HTML, CSS, Bootstrap, jQuery, Riot.js, CakePHP, Laravel \n● Data Visualization: Power BI, DAX, Power Query \n● Data Modelling: DAX, Data Transformation and Cleaning (Power Query) \n● Data Integration & Management: SQL Server, PostgreSQL, Data Import (Excel, SQL Server, \nCSV) \n● Frameworks & Tools: .NET Framework, Xamarin.Forms, MVC, pgAdmin4, FileZilla, VS \nCode \n● Version Control: Git, Bitbucket, Tortoise SVN \n● Project Management & Collaboration: ClickUp, Redmine, WinMerge, VMware \n● Other Skills: Problem-solving, adapting, team collaboration,technical \ndocumentation \n \n \nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE \nSoftware Development Intern (Part-time) \nAuckland Institute of Studies, Auckland | Aug 2024 – Dec 2024 \n \n● Data Analysis and Visualization: Created and improved Power BI dashboards, refining \nmeasures and enhancing performance for university management. \n● Team Collaboration: Collaborated with team members to understand data requirements and \ntranslate them into actionable visual insights. \n● Data Cleaning and Preparation: Used Power Query and DAX for data transformation and \nmodeling to ensure accurate and effective data visualization. \n \nSoftware Developer (WFH | Full-time) \nSagbrain Corporation, Auckland | 2022 - 2025 \n \n● Web Development: Developed and maintained web applications using Laravel, PHP, HTML, \nCSS, and JavaScript. \n● Team Collaboration: Worked closely with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality \nsoftware solutions; recognized twice for exceptional performance. \n● Problem Solving: Identified and resolved bugs, enhancing application performance and reliability. \n \nSoftware Developer (Full-time) \nSouthern Cross Systems, Japan | 2019 - 2022 \n \n● .NET Development: Developed client projects using .NET framework, focusing on \nperformance optimization and responsive design. \n● Web Design: Developed responsive web pages using HTML, CSS, and Bootstrap. \n● Data Analysis: Assisted in data analysis tasks to support business decision-making. \n \nEDUCATION \nBachelor of Science in Computer Science \nBRAC University | 2015-2018 | CGPA: 3.79/4.00 \n\nMORE \n \nPROJECT INVOLVED \nStudent Performance Dashboard | 2024 \n● Objective: Provide insights on student performance, retention rates, and academic trends for \nuniversity management. \n● Contributions: Refined an existing Student Performance Dashboard for university \nmanagement by correcting inaccurate measures and data inconsistencies. \n● Technologies: Power BI for data visualization, Data modelling using DAX, Data Integration by \nimporting data from Excel, SQL server, usage of tools like SQL Server Management Studio \nCRM Web Application | 2024 \n● Objective: Manage customer relationships within the bioscience industry. \n● Contributions: Identify and resolve bugs, implement updates, and improve workflow, reducing \norder processing time by 25%. \n● Technologies: Laravel, PostgreSQL, pgAdmin4, JavaScript, CSS3/HTML5, Bootstrap5. \nOrder EDI Platform | 2023 \n● Objective: Facilitate ordering between customers and dealers in the bioscience industry. \n● Contributions: Enhance and implement new features, ensuring ongoing functionality. \n● Technologies: CakePHP, Riot.js, PostgreSQL, CSS3/HTML5, Bootstrap5. \nDesktop Application Upgrade | 2022 \n● Objective: Upgrade raw materials management application for supply chain management. \n● Contributions: Assist in migration from VB5 to VB.NET, refactoring code for .NET features. \n● Technologies: VB.NET, VB5, Spread Component, SQL Server, .NET Framework. \n \nXamarin App enhancement | 2022 \n● Objective: Enhance a Xamarin app for medical professionals to check patient history. \n● Contributions: Implement an in-app browser to improve user experience. \n● Technologies: Xamarin.Forms, C#, WebView. \n \nExcel File Automation with VB Script (2021) \n● Objective: Automate file save and download operations from Excel files. \n● Contributions: Develop VB scripts, improving data management efficiency. \n● Technologies: Visual Basic (VB), Excel VBA, Microsoft Excel, Windows OS. \n \n \nHOBBIES \n● Cycling, Kickboxing, Movies, art and trying new things \n \n \nREFERENCES \n● Available upon request \n ', '2026-01-28 09:48:00'),
(11, 16, '1770614223233.pdf', 'uploads/resumes/1770614223233.pdf', '\n\n \nERIC DE LEON CERVAS \n Mount Eden, Auckland, New Zealand \nMobile:  +64  274998054 I Email:  eric.cervas@yahoo.com   \nLinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/eric-cervas-cpa-41b662b8/ \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nFinance  and  accounting  professional  with  14+  years  of  experience  across  financial  reporting, \nbudgeting,  forecasting,  taxation,  treasury,  and  ERP  systems.  Strong  analytical  capability  with \nexpertise  in  IFRS,  internal  controls,  and  process  improvement.  Currently  completing  an  MBA \nmajor  in  Finance  at  Auckland  Institute  of  Studies  and  seeking  a  finance  internship  to  apply \nadvanced  learning  in  financial  risk  management,  valuation,  liquidity  analysis,  and  strategic \nfinancial decision‑making. \n \nSKILLS \n• Financial Reporting & IFRS Compliance                  • Financial Analysis & Risk Assessment \n• Budgeting, Forecasting & Variance Analysis            • Treasury & Cashflow Management \n• ERP Systems (Oracle), Xero, Advanced Excel          • Taxation & Regulatory Compliance \n• Process Improvement & Systems Enhancement        • Corporate Finance & Valuation \n• Leadership, Communication & Team Collaboration   • Time Management &Organisational Skills   \n______________________________________________________________________________ \nWORK HISTORY \nACCOUNTANT / BOOKKEEPER \nWC Ruiz Accounting, Auditing & Tax Consultancy Services \n(https://www.facebook.com/CERVASAccountingFirm8/about/)IPhilippines I Dec. 2023-Oct. 2024 \nResponsibilities: \n• Managed financial records, general ledger, and full-cycle accounting. \n• Prepared financial statements, budgets, and forecasts. \n• Conducted financial analysis and identified process improvement opportunities. \n• Ensured tax compliance for SME and corporate clients (IFRS-based). \n• Supported audit requirements and regulatory submissions. \n \nGENERAL ACCOUNTANT /FINANCE OFFICER \nArabian Homes Co. (https://arabian-homes.com/) I Saudi Arabia I May 2013-November 2023 \nResponsibilities: \n• Managed treasury, cashflow, credit control, and accounts reconciliation. \n• Prepared budgets, financial reports, and variance analysis. \n• Ensured accuracy of financial data in Oracle ERP. \n• Managed lease accounting, documentation, and customer financial portfolios. \n• Handled AP/AR, tax compliance, personnel records, and payroll. \n• Led process improvements to enhance financial accuracy and efficiency. \n \n \n\nSENIOR ACCOUNTANT  \nManabat & Co.-KPMG Philippines (https://kpmg.com/ph/en/home.html)IApril to December 2012 \nResponsibilities: \n• Managed client financial portfolios and reporting requirements. \n• Conducted reconciliation, loans processing, and controls evaluation. \n• Supported financial-system improvements and compliance reviews. \n \nAdditional Early Experience (2005- 2011) \n \nCOLLEGE INSTRUCTOR (Accounting & Business-Urdaneta City University (https://ucu.edu.ph/)  \nACCOUNTANT / BOOKKEEPER- Daroya & Co. CPA’s (http://www.daroya.com.ph/) \nACCOUNTING /ADMIN STAFF- S&F  Finance  Corporation/  International  Freeport  Traders  Inc. \nhttps://philippinecompanies.com/companyprofile/427321/s-f-finance-corporation;  \n(For full work experience description kindly check my LinkedIn account).  \n \nEDUCATION \nMaster of Business Administration-Major on Finance \nAuckland Institute of Studies, Auckland, New Zealand \nStart: October 2024      Expected completion: 2025 \n \nBachelor of Science in Accountancy \nUrdaneta City University  \nUrdaneta City, Philippines I Year 2000 to 2004 \n \nTRAININGS & CERTIFICATIONS \n• Xero Accounting Certificate \n• Continuing Professional Development (Accounting & Consultancy – NZ & PH) \n• Member, National Institute of Accounting Technicians (Philippines) \n• Member, Philippine Institute of Certified Public Accountants \n• Associate Member, Saudi Organization for Chartered & Professional Accountants \n• CPA Australia – Eligibility confirmed for associate membership \n \nINTEREST / HOBBIES \n• Puzzles and brain games            • Music and singing \n• Basketball and team sports       • Exploring parks and heritage sites \n______________________________________________________________________________ \nREFERENCES \nAvailable upon request  ', '2026-02-09 05:17:03'),
(12, 16, '1770617039386.pdf', 'uploads/resumes/1770617039386.pdf', '\n\n \nERIC DE LEON CERVAS \n Mount Eden, Auckland, New Zealand \nMobile:  +64  274998054 I Email:  eric.cervas@yahoo.com   \nLinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/in/eric-cervas-cpa-41b662b8/ \n \nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY \nI am a finance and accounting professional with 14+ years of expertise across financial reporting, \nbudgeting, forecasting, taxation, treasury, and ERP financial systems. Skilled in financial analysis, \nrisk assessment, and process improvement, with strong knowledge of IFRS and internal controls. \nI  am  currently  studying at   Auckland  Institute of  Studies for Master of  Business  Administration \n(MBA -major  in  Finance)  and  seeking  a  finance  internship  opportunity  to  apply  my  advanced \nacademic learning in areas such as financial risk management, valuation, liquidity analysis, and \nstrategic financial decision-making. \n \nSKILLS \n• Financial Reporting & IFRS Compliance                       • Budgeting & Variance Analysis \n• Financial Analysis & Forecasting                                   • Internal Controls & Compliance \n• ERP Systems (Oracle), Xero, Advanced Excel              • Taxation & Regulatory Requirements \n• Process Improvement & Systems Enhancement             • Corporate Finance & Valuation \n• Leadership, Communication & Team Collaboration      • Risk Assessment \n• Time Management & Organisational Skills                    • Treasury & Cashflow Management \n______________________________________________________________________________ \nWORK HISTORY \nACCOUNTANT / BOOKKEEPER \nWC Ruiz Accounting, Auditing & Tax Consultancy Services \n(https://www.facebook.com/CERVASAccountingFirm8/about/)IPhilippines I Dec. 2023-Oct. 2024 \nResponsibilities: \n• Managed financial records, general ledger, and full-cycle accounting. \n• Prepared financial statements, budgets, and forecasts. \n• Conducted financial analysis and identified process improvement opportunities. \n• Ensured tax compliance for SME and corporate clients (IFRS-based). \n• Supported audit requirements and regulatory submissions. \n \nGENERAL ACCOUNTANT /FINANCE OFFICER \nArabian Homes Co. (https://arabian-homes.com/) I Saudi Arabia I May 2013-November 2023 \nResponsibilities: \n• Managed treasury, cashflow, credit control, and accounts reconciliation. \n• Prepared budgets, financial reports, and variance analysis. \n• Ensured accuracy of financial data in Oracle ERP. \n• Managed lease accounting, documentation, and customer financial portfolios. \n• Handled AP/AR, tax compliance, personnel records, and payroll. \n• Led process improvements to enhance financial accuracy and efficiency. \n\n \nSENIOR ACCOUNTANT  \nManabat & Co.-KPMG Philippines (https://kpmg.com/ph/en/home.html)IApril to December 2012 \nResponsibilities: \n• Managed client financial portfolios. \n• Conducted reconciliation, loans processing, and controls evaluation. \n• Supported financial-system improvements. \n \nCOLLEGE INSTRUCTOR (Accounting & Business) \nUrdaneta City University (https://ucu.edu.ph/)I Philippines I June to October 2011  \n \nBOOKKEEPER \nDaroya & Co. CPA’s (http://www.daroya.com.ph/)  I Philippines I October 2009-August 2010 \n \nAdditional Early Experience \nACCOUNTING STAFF S&F Finance Corporation/ International Freeport Traders Inc. (2008- 2009) \nhttps://philippinecompanies.com/companyprofile/427321/s-f-finance-corporation;  \n(For full work experience description kindly check my LinkedIn account).  \n \nEDUCATION \nMaster of Business Administration-Major on Finance \nAuckland Institute of Studies, Auckland, New Zealand \nStart: October 2024      Expected completion: 2025 \n \nBachelor of Science in Accountancy \nUrdaneta City University  \nUrdaneta City, Philippines I Year 2000 to 2004 \n \nTRAININGS & CERTIFICATIONS \n• Xero Accounting Certificate \n• Continuing Professional Development (Accounting & Consultancy – NZ & PH) \n• Member, National Institute of Accounting Technicians \n• Member, Philippine Institute of Certified Public Accountants \n• Associate Member, Saudi Organization for Chartered & Professional Accountants \n• CPA Australia – Eligibility confirmed for associate membership \n \nINTEREST / HOBBIES \n• Solving puzzles and brain games                                • Singing and enjoying music \n• Playing basketball and engaging in team sports       • Exploring parks and historical heritage sites \n• Socializing and connecting with friends via social media \n______________________________________________________________________________ \nREFERENCES \nAvailable upon request  ', '2026-02-09 06:03:59'),
(13, 16, '1771394933830.docx', 'uploads/resumes/1771394933830.docx', 'Uploaded file: Alyssa - CV.docx', '2026-02-18 06:08:53'),
(14, 16, '1771395041562.pdf', 'uploads/resumes/1771395041562.pdf', '\n\nAFSARY \nPhone: +64 22 508 6961 | Email: afsary.92@gmail.com |  \nLinkedIn: linkedin.com/in/afsary \nLocation: 5B Freeman Way, Manukau, Auckland, New Zealand \n \nProfessional Summary \nResults-driven  operations  and  supply  chain  professional  with  over  seven  years’ \nexperience across supply chain coordination and accounting functions. Strong expertise \nin  inventory  management,  ERP  systems,  demand  forecasting,  and  financial  reporting. \nProven ability to support efficient operations while ensuring accuracy, compliance, and \ndata-driven decision-making.\n \nKey Skills \n Supply chain coordination and logistics planning \n Inventory management and demand forecasting \n Transportation, warehousing, and distribution management \n ERP systems and data accuracy \n Cross-functional team collaboration \n Financial record-keeping and reporting \n Accounts payable and receivable management \n Payroll support and invoice processing \n Attention to detail and compliance with internal controls \n \n \nEducation \nMaster of Business Administration (Operations & Logistics). \nAuckland Institute of Studies, Auckland, New Zealand \n01.02.2025-31.07.2026. \n \nBachelor of Business Administration (Accounting and Finance) \nAmerican International University-Bangladesh. \nFrom 2012-2016. \n \n \n \n\nWork Experience \nSupply Chain Coordinator – Smart Technologies BD Ltd (https://smartbd.com/). \n2020 – 2023  \n• Planned and coordinated transportation, warehousing, and distribution activities to \nensure smooth business operations \n• Monitored stock levels, forecasted demand, and optimized inventory storage and \nmovement \n• Used ERP systems to maintain accurate supply and inventory records \n• Supported cross-functional teams to improve supply chain efficiency and service \ndelivery \nAccountant – Smart Technologies BD Ltd, Bangladesh (https://smartbd.com/) \n2016 – 2020 \n• Posted journal entries and maintained accurate financial records \n• Managed accounts receivable and payable, invoices, and payments \n• Assisted with payroll processing and monthly reporting \n• Ensured compliance with accounting standards and internal controls \n \nCertifications & Training \n• Trade Guidelines and Automation (2017) \n• Effective Corporate Communication Training (2020) \n \nCommunity & Volunteer Experience \nVolunteer – Student Defence, Bangladesh (2014) \n• Distributed care packages for students \n• Updated and maintained the Student Defence website \n \nHobbies \n• Reading \n• Travelling \n \n \nReferences \n \n• Available on request ', '2026-02-18 06:10:42');

